<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Bessi</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Thracian highland people of the Rhodopes and Haemus, keepers of a famous oracle of Dionysus and stubborn rebels against Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, writing in the 5th century BCE, names the Bessi as the priests of the oracle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysus">Dionysus</a> in the mountains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrae">Satrae</a>. By later centuries they were a distinct people of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Hebrus</a> (Maritsa) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodope-mountains">Rhodope</a> ranges in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A loose tribal people of mountain country, the Bessi combined herding, mining and raiding. Their religious standing as guardians of the Dionysian sanctuary gave them prestige among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thracians">Thracians</a>. They clashed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/odrysian-kingdom">Odrysian Kingdom</a> and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, and later raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-roman-province">Roman Macedonia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a> subdued them in 29 BCE, but in 11 BCE the priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vologases-thracian-priest">Vologases</a> led a major revolt that took years to crush. Their name survived under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and a Bessian language was reportedly still used in monastic worship in the 6th century CE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bessi.jpg" alt="Bessi" width="320" height="205"><figcaption>Image: Megistias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OdrysianKingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vologases</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Thracian polytheism (cult of Dionysus)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Thracian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bessians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-264&amp;focus=bessi" aria-label="Bessi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5289 666 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bessi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5609 922h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5609 922h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Bulgaria. <a href="/atlas?year=-264&amp;focus=bessi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

